{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security Deposit Law deposit cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may take no more than one and one-half times one month's rent as a security deposit, may raise it by at most 10% a year, and must return it with interest within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; 10% annual increase cap","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey; the deposit-account and interest provisions do not apply to seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"A landlord need not collect a deposit at all; seasonal use or rental of 125 consecutive days or fewer is exempt from the deposit-account provisions, and seasonal or migrant farm worker housing is not seasonal use.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, together with court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic-violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and, within three business days, notify the tenant in writing where it may be picked up.","key_value":"15 business days to return; 3 business days to notify","coverage_conditions":"Residential leases terminated by a domestic violence victim under the Safe Housing Act; the law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"lease terminated by a domestic violence victim"},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
